                                                        | ;; Genes metformin interacts with that are ALSO associated with type 2 diabetes.
                                                        | ;;
                                                        | ;; Metformin expands to 120 KG2 ids -> too many to inline, so it gets one membership
                                                        | ;; relation (one stage).  T2D expands to 9 ids -> inlined as literals across many rules
                                                        | ;; sharing the head `result`, which stays a single stage.
                                                        | ;;
                                                        | ;; CRITICAL: the metformin-side gene (g) and the T2D-side gene (g2) are derived
                                                        | ;; independently and land in different vocabularies (NCBIGene vs UniProtKB vs HGNC vs
                                                        | ;; UMLS).  Joining them on the raw id returns 0 rows.  They are joined on the canonical
                                                        | ;; key k from kg2_norm, and a real KG2 id is returned alongside k so it can be named.
